; qlfile -- qlot dependency manifest for sext
; Run: qlot install
;
; Resolved by direct verification -- a real `qlot install` run against this
; exact file, not just checking dist metadata. See CLAUDE.md, "Issue #3
; resolution" and "Issue #7 notes" for the full evidence trail. Summary:
;
;   - `ql <name>` takes a Quicklisp PROJECT name (per the dist's
;     releases.txt), not necessarily an ASDF SYSTEM name -- the two only
;     coincide when a release's primary system shares the release's name.
;     An earlier version of this file got this wrong for three entries,
;     confirmed only by a live `qlot install` actually failing (checking
;     dist metadata by hand wasn't enough to catch it, since systems.txt
;     lists every system a release provides without making the
;     project/system distinction obvious):
;       - com.inuoe.jzon (the ASDF system) is shipped by the "jzon"
;         project (releases.txt: project jzon ships src/com.inuoe.jzon.asd)
;       - eclector-concrete-syntax-tree is shipped by the "eclector"
;         project, in the SAME release tarball as eclector itself
;         (releases.txt: project eclector ships both eclector.asd and
;         eclector-concrete-syntax-tree.asd) -- no separate qlfile line
;         needed once `ql eclector` is present; ASDF finds it on disk.
;       - khazern-extrinsic is shipped by the "khazern" project, same
;         situation (releases.txt: project khazern ships both khazern.asd
;         and khazern-extrinsic.asd) -- no separate line needed once
;         `ql khazern` is present.
;     Fixed: `ql com.inuoe.jzon` -> `ql jzon`; the eclector-concrete-syntax-
;     tree and khazern-extrinsic lines removed as redundant. sext.asd's own
;     :depends-on correctly keeps the ASDF SYSTEM names (com.inuoe.jzon,
;     eclector-concrete-syntax-tree, khazern-extrinsic) -- that's a
;     different namespace (ASDF system names) and was never the bug; only
;     this file's PROJECT-name lookups were wrong.
;   - concrete-syntax-tree, fiveam, closer-mop: project name and the
;     system name sext needs coincide, no special-casing needed.
;   - cleavir-ctype (the AST converter's type-representation protocol)
;     ships its own complete default implementation as part of Cleavir
;     itself (Ctype/default.lisp, unconditionally loaded) -- no separate
;     `ctype`/`ctype/tfun` library dependency needed. An earlier version
;     of this manifest listed `ctype`/`ctype/tfun` on the mistaken
;     assumption that Cleavir's own Example/ frontend's choice of backend
;     was required; see CLAUDE.md, "Issue #5 notes" for the full story.
;   - trivial-json-codec/shasht (a CLOS-aware JSON encoding layer) are
;     NOT needed either, for the same class of reason: Cleavir already
;     ships its own canonical "what's interesting about this AST node"
;     protocol, CLEAVIR-IO:SAVE-INFO, which sext's walker (src/walker.lisp)
;     uses directly to fully flatten AST objects to plain data before
;     any JSON library sees them -- so only a thin plain-data JSON writer
;     is needed, and com.inuoe.jzon already covers that. See
;     src/walker.lisp's file header for the full evidence trail.
;   - Cleavir (cleavir-cst-to-ast, cleavir-ast, and the rest of the
;     cleavir-* family) is NOT in Quicklisp or Ultralisp (verified: zero
;     matches in either dist's systems.txt/releases.txt). It ships only
;     as a single monorepo at the URL below; every cleavir-*.asd file
;     lives in its own subdirectory, so the registry needs each
;     subdirectory pushed, not just the repo root.

ql fiveam
ql jzon
ql concrete-syntax-tree
ql eclector
ql khazern

git cleavir https://github.com/s-expressionists/Cleavir.git

ultralisp 40ants-doc
